course: dictionary
lesson: 8252
title: Rhythm in words and life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rhythm is a regular, repeated pattern of beats or sounds. You can hear it in music, in poems and in your own heartbeat. When your teacher says «clap the rhythm», she means clap the pattern of beats, not just any noise.
explain: Poems have rhythm too. Clap this line: «HICK-o-ry, DICK-o-ry, DOCK, the MOUSE ran UP the CLOCK.» The capital letters are the strong beats, and the small letters are the weak ones. The strong and weak pattern repeats, so you can march to it like a drum.
explain: Rhythm can match the meaning of a poem. In Robert Louis Stevenson's train poem, «Faster than fairies, faster than witches» has a quick beat that rattles along like wheels on a track. A sad poem is read slowly and softly, so its rhythm sounds different.
explain: Rhythm also means a pattern in life and nature, like day and night or the seasons. Your body clock, called a circadian rhythm, runs on about 24 hours, matching one spin of the Earth.
fact: Rhythm is a regular, repeated pattern of beats or sounds.
fact: A rhythm can be a regular pattern in life or nature, like day and night or the seasons.
fact: In poetry, rhythm is the pattern of strong and weak sounds that you can clap.
fact: «Rhythm» can match the meaning of a poem: a quick beat can feel fast and lively, and a slow beat can feel calm or sad.
fact: The indri is the biggest living lemur, and scientists found rhythms in indri songs a little like music.
exercise: What is a rhythm? | *A regular, repeated pattern of beats or sounds | A word that rhymes with another | A colour in a picture | A single loud noise
exercise: In «Faster than fairies, faster than witches», the quick beat rattles along like what? | A sleepy cat curled up | *Wheels on a track | A slow, soft lullaby
exercise: Which is an example of a rhythm in life or nature? | *Day and night, coming back again and again | A single surprise | A word you have never heard
test: The body clock is called a circadian rhythm because it runs on about how many hours? | *24 hours | 12 hours | 1 hour | 100 hours
test: Free verse is poetry without regular rhyme, so what does a free verse poem still use? | Only a title | Music only | Numbers only | *Rhythm, line breaks and imagery
exam: The indri's song has rhythms a little like what? | Traffic noise | *Music | Silence | A dripping tap
